From d14514c66cb9721b54318850796c005c446d76d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Suren Baghdasaryan <surenb@google.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Mar 2026 00:08:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mm/vmscan: prevent MGLRU reclaim from pinning address space

[ Backport of d14514c66cb9 from 7.1 ]

When shrinking lruvec, MGLRU pins the address space (mmget) before
walking it. That delays releasing a dying process: process_mrelease()
and the oom-reaper see an elevated mm->mm_users and skip the mm.
On Android this shows up as killed apps holding memory for seconds
while kswapd is scanning them.

Only the mm_struct needs to stay alive for mmap_read_lock + mm_mt
walk. Replace mmget_not_zero/mmput_async with mmgrab/mmdrop.

[ Adapted for OnePlus 6.1.141 OKI: helper is still should_skip_mm()
  rather than get_next_mm(). ]

Fixes: bd74fdaea146 ("mm: multi-gen LRU: support page table walks")
Signed-off-by: Suren Baghdasaryan <surenb@google.com>
---
 mm/vmscan.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -3799,7 +3799,8 @@ static bool should_skip_mm(struct mm_struct *mm, struct lru_gen_mm_walk *walk)
 	if (size < MIN_LRU_BATCH)
 		return true;
 
-	return !mmget_not_zero(mm);
+	mmgrab(mm);
+	return false;
 }
 
 static bool iterate_mm_list(struct lruvec *lruvec, struct lru_gen_mm_walk *walk,
@@ -3863,7 +3864,7 @@ static bool iterate_mm_list(struct lruvec *lruvec, struct lru_gen_mm_walk *walk,
 		reset_bloom_filter(lruvec, walk->max_seq + 1);
 
 	if (*iter)
-		mmput_async(*iter);
+		mmdrop(*iter);
 
 	*iter = mm;
 
